1
00:00:00,146 --> 00:00:01,782
You're in space.

2
00:00:01,782 --> 00:00:02,920
No suit.

3
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:03,950
You've got about

4
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:05,200
fifteen seconds.

5
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,200
Your instinct?

6
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,120
Hold your breath.

7
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:08,100
WRONG.

8
00:00:08,130 --> 00:00:09,600
Breathe OUT,

9
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:10,860
with him...

10
00:00:11,513 --> 00:00:12,800
all of it...

11
00:00:13,413 --> 00:00:14,367
now.

12
00:00:14,410 --> 00:00:15,113
Holding it in

13
00:00:15,113 --> 00:00:17,259
could tear your lungs.

14
00:00:17,549 --> 00:00:18,049
All he wanted

15
00:00:18,049 --> 00:00:18,689
was a selfie

16
00:00:18,689 --> 00:00:20,289
for his niece, Pip.

17
00:00:20,289 --> 00:00:20,849
Without the helmet.

18
00:00:20,849 --> 00:00:21,729
"You look like

19
00:00:21,729 --> 00:00:23,009
a goldfish,"

20
00:00:23,059 --> 00:00:23,967
she said.

21
00:00:24,010 --> 00:00:24,479
So he pressed

22
00:00:24,479 --> 00:00:25,766
the button marked

23
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,170
DEPRESS...

24
00:00:27,302 --> 00:00:28,433
thinking it meant

25
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:30,050
"take the picture."

26
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:32,230
Now, second by second,

27
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:33,780
here's what your body does...

28
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:34,800
and how long

29
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,530
a rescue has.

30
00:00:36,730 --> 00:00:37,670
Second one.

31
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:38,613
Good news:

32
00:00:38,613 --> 00:00:39,840
you don't explode.

33
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:41,467
That's just the movies.

34
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:42,458
Your skin is

35
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:43,933
tougher than that.

36
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:45,080
Second two.

37
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,400
The air is gone...

38
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,800
and so is the sound.

39
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:49,380
The alarm is screaming.

40
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:50,533
He can't hear a thing.

41
00:00:52,515 --> 00:00:53,720
Is he freezing?

42
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:54,490
Not yet.

43
00:00:54,490 --> 00:00:55,927
Space is cold,

44
00:00:55,927 --> 00:00:56,820
but empty:

45
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:57,772
there's nothing to carry

46
00:00:57,772 --> 00:00:59,000
his heat away.

47
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:00,770
Space is basically...

48
00:01:00,770 --> 00:01:02,640
a giant thermos.

49
00:01:02,723 --> 00:01:03,740
But his spit?

50
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:04,261
Touch your tongue

51
00:01:04,261 --> 00:01:05,240
to your lip.

52
00:01:05,240 --> 00:01:05,920
Feel that?

53
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:06,988
Second five:

54
00:01:06,988 --> 00:01:08,600
his is boiling.

55
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:09,404
With no air

56
00:01:09,404 --> 00:01:10,470
pressing on it,

57
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:11,285
water boils

58
00:01:11,285 --> 00:01:12,890
at body temperature.

59
00:01:12,890 --> 00:01:13,868
His spit.

60
00:01:13,868 --> 00:01:15,024
His tears.

61
00:01:15,024 --> 00:01:16,218
And all that boiling

62
00:01:16,218 --> 00:01:17,451
steals heat...

63
00:01:17,451 --> 00:01:19,180
so his mouth gets cold.

64
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:20,933
Almost freezing.

65
00:01:20,964 --> 00:01:22,024
Second ten.

66
00:01:22,024 --> 00:01:22,624
The real danger

67
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:24,224
is in here.

68
00:01:24,224 --> 00:01:25,424
His lungs are empty,

69
00:01:25,424 --> 00:01:26,044
so the oxygen

70
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:26,784
in his blood

71
00:01:26,784 --> 00:01:28,324
pours OUT...

72
00:01:28,324 --> 00:01:29,444
the wrong way.

73
00:01:29,515 --> 00:01:30,645
And that blood,

74
00:01:30,645 --> 00:01:31,297
with almost

75
00:01:31,297 --> 00:01:32,747
nothing left in it,

76
00:01:32,747 --> 00:01:33,737
is on its way

77
00:01:33,737 --> 00:01:35,033
to his brain.

78
00:01:35,063 --> 00:01:36,590
Fourteen...

79
00:01:37,703 --> 00:01:38,990
fifteen...

80
00:01:39,910 --> 00:01:40,600
lights out.

81
00:01:42,148 --> 00:01:43,018
He's out.

82
00:01:43,298 --> 00:01:44,378
Not dead...

83
00:01:44,378 --> 00:01:45,078
out.

84
00:01:45,338 --> 00:01:46,258
And now,

85
00:01:46,378 --> 00:01:48,058
a different clock starts.

86
00:01:48,187 --> 00:01:48,847
Ball,

87
00:01:48,847 --> 00:01:50,057
the camera drone,

88
00:01:50,057 --> 00:01:51,307
wants to help.

89
00:01:51,507 --> 00:01:51,907
But its fans

90
00:01:51,867 --> 00:01:52,547
need air

91
00:01:52,547 --> 00:01:53,867
to push against.

92
00:01:54,027 --> 00:01:54,987
Right now,

93
00:01:54,987 --> 00:01:56,337
Ball is just...

94
00:01:56,337 --> 00:01:57,187
a ball.

95
00:01:57,522 --> 00:01:58,472
Down the hall,

96
00:01:58,472 --> 00:01:59,162
the alarm reaches

97
00:01:59,162 --> 00:02:00,432
his big sister,

98
00:02:00,432 --> 00:02:01,282
the commander.

99
00:02:01,662 --> 00:02:02,642
She's been rescuing him

100
00:02:02,642 --> 00:02:03,982
since he was four.

101
00:02:04,169 --> 00:02:05,274
Second twenty.

102
00:02:05,274 --> 00:02:06,298
The water in his body

103
00:02:06,298 --> 00:02:07,790
is turning to gas.

104
00:02:07,790 --> 00:02:08,940
He's swelling...

105
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:10,500
like his bag of chips.

106
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:12,165
Pinch the skin

107
00:02:12,165 --> 00:02:13,640
on the back of your hand.

108
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:14,458
Let go.

109
00:02:14,458 --> 00:02:15,263
It snaps back,

110
00:02:15,263 --> 00:02:15,750
right?

111
00:02:15,750 --> 00:02:16,449
That's what's

112
00:02:16,449 --> 00:02:18,067
holding him together.

113
00:02:18,090 --> 00:02:19,478
In 1960,

114
00:02:19,478 --> 00:02:20,174
a pilot named

115
00:02:20,174 --> 00:02:21,066
Joe Kittinger

116
00:02:21,066 --> 00:02:21,866
rode a balloon

117
00:02:21,866 --> 00:02:23,767
nineteen miles up.

118
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:24,577
One of his gloves

119
00:02:24,577 --> 00:02:25,614
failed.

120
00:02:25,614 --> 00:02:26,800
His hand swelled

121
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,800
to twice its size...

122
00:02:28,830 --> 00:02:29,635
and three hours

123
00:02:29,635 --> 00:02:30,818
after he landed,

124
00:02:30,818 --> 00:02:32,600
the swelling was gone.

125
00:02:32,653 --> 00:02:33,833
Second thirty.

126
00:02:33,853 --> 00:02:34,253
What does this

127
00:02:34,173 --> 00:02:35,393
feel like?

128
00:02:35,393 --> 00:02:36,633
One man knows.

129
00:02:37,053 --> 00:02:38,533
In 1966,

130
00:02:38,613 --> 00:02:39,173
Jim LeBlanc

131
00:02:39,173 --> 00:02:40,413
was testing a spacesuit

132
00:02:40,413 --> 00:02:40,953
in a NASA

133
00:02:40,953 --> 00:02:42,373
vacuum chamber,

134
00:02:42,373 --> 00:02:43,133
when its air hose

135
00:02:43,133 --> 00:02:44,233
came loose.

136
00:02:44,439 --> 00:02:44,919
He stayed awake

137
00:02:44,919 --> 00:02:45,379
for about

138
00:02:45,379 --> 00:02:46,959
fourteen seconds.

139
00:02:47,019 --> 00:02:47,479
The last thing

140
00:02:47,479 --> 00:02:48,419
he remembered?

141
00:02:48,539 --> 00:02:50,059
The spit on his tongue...

142
00:02:50,059 --> 00:02:51,359
starting to bubble.

143
00:02:51,546 --> 00:02:52,266
They pumped the air

144
00:02:52,266 --> 00:02:53,256
back in,

145
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:53,946
fast.

146
00:02:54,126 --> 00:02:55,266
And he was fine.

147
00:02:55,266 --> 00:02:56,026
He just couldn't

148
00:02:56,026 --> 00:02:57,026
taste much...

149
00:02:57,026 --> 00:02:58,326
for four days.

150
00:02:58,765 --> 00:03:00,450
Second forty-five.

151
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,405
Every bit of gas

152
00:03:01,405 --> 00:03:02,050
in his gut

153
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:03,720
is swelling too.

154
00:03:04,515 --> 00:03:05,070
Yes.

155
00:03:05,070 --> 00:03:06,545
That gas.

156
00:03:06,665 --> 00:03:07,952
Second sixty.

157
00:03:07,952 --> 00:03:08,550
His heart

158
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:09,810
is still beating...

159
00:03:09,810 --> 00:03:10,810
but slower,

160
00:03:10,810 --> 00:03:12,033
and slower.

161
00:03:12,062 --> 00:03:12,532
So how long

162
00:03:12,532 --> 00:03:13,612
does he have?

163
00:03:13,712 --> 00:03:14,112
Nobody's allowed

164
00:03:14,052 --> 00:03:14,632
to test that

165
00:03:14,632 --> 00:03:15,692
on a person.

166
00:03:15,912 --> 00:03:16,872
In the nineteen-sixties,

167
00:03:16,872 --> 00:03:17,692
they tested it

168
00:03:17,692 --> 00:03:18,772
on animals.

169
00:03:19,030 --> 00:03:19,606
Every dog

170
00:03:19,606 --> 00:03:20,240
brought back

171
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,910
within ninety seconds

172
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:22,690
lived.

173
00:03:22,690 --> 00:03:23,308
After about

174
00:03:23,308 --> 00:03:24,376
three minutes...

175
00:03:24,376 --> 00:03:25,700
most didn't.

176
00:03:25,745 --> 00:03:27,305
In 1971,

177
00:03:27,595 --> 00:03:28,425
a valve opened

178
00:03:28,425 --> 00:03:29,985
on a Soyuz capsule,

179
00:03:30,145 --> 00:03:31,325
on its way home.

180
00:03:31,665 --> 00:03:32,605
Its three cosmonauts

181
00:03:32,605 --> 00:03:34,425
are still the only people

182
00:03:34,425 --> 00:03:35,625
who ever died

183
00:03:35,625 --> 00:03:36,845
in space.

184
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:38,780
Second eighty.

185
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:39,500
Her hand

186
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:41,000
hits REPRESS.

187
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:45,285
Second ninety.

188
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:46,720
Air.

189
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:48,050
And like

190
00:03:48,050 --> 00:03:49,570
Jim LeBlanc...

191
00:03:49,830 --> 00:03:51,130
he wakes up.

192
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:52,810
Hold out your hand.

193
00:03:52,830 --> 00:03:53,450
Right now,

194
00:03:53,450 --> 00:03:54,770
the air is pressing on it

195
00:03:54,770 --> 00:03:55,270
with the weight

196
00:03:55,270 --> 00:03:56,490
of a grown-up.

197
00:03:56,490 --> 00:03:57,580
You don't feel it,

198
00:03:57,580 --> 00:03:58,170
because your body

199
00:03:58,170 --> 00:03:58,810
pushes back

200
00:03:58,810 --> 00:04:00,210
just as hard.

201
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:01,120
Space doesn't

202
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:02,283
pull you apart.

203
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:03,083
It just stops

204
00:04:03,083 --> 00:04:04,770
holding you together.

205
00:04:04,904 --> 00:04:05,507
He was puffy

206
00:04:05,507 --> 00:04:06,900
for a couple of days.

207
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:07,829
His pride...

208
00:04:07,829 --> 00:04:09,300
a lot longer.

209
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:09,940
So:

210
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:11,190
one more selfie.

211
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,060
Helmet on.

212
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:12,891
Goldfish bowl

213
00:04:12,891 --> 00:04:14,130
and all.

214
00:04:14,390 --> 00:04:15,650
Turns out...

215
00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:16,342
we all live

216
00:04:16,342 --> 00:04:18,122
in a goldfish bowl.

217
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:19,542
Ours is just

218
00:04:19,542 --> 00:04:20,980
very big...

219
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:22,633
and very thin.

220
00:04:25,270 --> 00:04:26,260
Next week:

221
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:27,340
what happens if you

222
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:29,620
stop brushing your teeth.

223
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:30,610
Subscribe...

224
00:04:30,610 --> 00:04:31,010
and keep

225
00:04:30,948 --> 00:04:32,346
your helmet on.

